From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0394-upstream-05-maps-on-the-back.patch

Source: 0394-upstream-05-maps-on-the-back.patch
gpu_thread: EDEN_NX2_MAP_ON_BACK=1 runs GPU memory maps on the split's back

Port of the gpu_thread.cpp part of Djihads80/Eglantine 3087c1cf07 (kraibse, from Duck912 e3d8e9c605,
#70, branch fix/oot-blackscreen, 2026-11-05). GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

The source commit: the front used back-owned state after a drain. A drained back still submits from
its idle hook (Scheduler::FlushDeferred), so a download recorded by the front met an empty command
chunk: a read at null+0x10 in BufferCacheRuntime::CopyBuffer. The other sites of that commit are in
this core already (0041, split-1 to split-3). Maps are the one left: UnmapMemory downloads, and
run->func() still runs on the front after split.Drain().

With the switch ThreadManager::Run wraps the map: the front runs the wrapper after its drain, as
before, and the wrapper sends the map to the back and waits. The order is unchanged. Done there, not
in the loop, so it stays clear of lichii-gpu-0210's Drain line.

rebase-02 (EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_QUIET=1) closes the same race another way, by waiting for the idle hook.
Its note warns that a WriteMemory from MapInOrder on the front keeps no GPU bytes beside it; run on
the back, the owner check passes and it does. Both can be set.

Changed from the source: behind the switch. Nothing on the map path calls Drain, which would hang on
the back: read, not run. Unset, nothing changes.

Runs on the PS5: same core path. Pool memory: none.

Co-authored-by: kraibse <33869366+kraibse@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: Duck912 <350528965+Duck912@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/gpu_thread.cpp b/src/video_core/gpu_thread.cpp
index 403fb3c61f..40be436f07 100644
--- a/src/video_core/gpu_thread.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/gpu_thread.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
 #include <chrono>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <thread>
 
 #include "common/assert.h"
@@ -169,6 +170,24 @@ void ThreadManager::TickGPU(bool is_async) {
 }
 
 void ThreadManager::Run(std::function<void()>&& func, bool is_async, bool before_later_reads) {
+    // EDEN_NX2_MAP_ON_BACK=1: GPU memory maps unmap caches (UnmapMemory downloads), the back's state,
+    // and a drained back still submits from its idle hook. The front runs this wrapper after its
+    // drain, as it would the map: the map itself goes to the back, and the front waits for it.
+    static const bool map_on_back = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_MAP_ON_BACK");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    if (before_later_reads && map_on_back) {
+        func = [work = std::move(func)]() mutable {
+            auto& split = VideoCommon::GpuSplit::Get();
+            if (split.Active()) {
+                split.DeferFunction(std::move(work));
+                split.Drain();
+            } else {
+                work();
+            }
+        };
+    }
     PushCommand(RunCommand{std::move(func), before_later_reads}, false, is_async);
 }
 
